{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedStandardGeneric","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedStandardGeneric","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedStandardTableau"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordSYT_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordSYT_eq","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardGeneric.lean#L92-L95","doc":"`insertWordSYT` factors through the generic primitive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordPSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWordPSYT","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardGeneric.lean#L82-L90","doc":"**The insertion tableau `P(w)` as a standard Young tableau**, for a permutation\nword `w` (content `{1, …, n}`).  Together with `insertWordSYT` (the recording\ntableau `Q̃(w)`), this gives both halves of the RSK pair as standard tableaux. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.listStandardYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.listStandardYT","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardGeneric.lean#L29-L80","doc":"**Any standard-filled list tableau is a standard Young tableau.**  A list\ntableau with weakly-increasing rows, strictly-increasing columns, and content\n`{1, …, n}` realises as a `QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau` on its row-length\nshape; its entry map bijects the cells onto `Set.Icc 1 n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}